done	<str>Equip your facemask and enter the Smoke Dungeon west of Pollnivneach and east of the mirrors</str>
done	
done	<str>Light the 4 standing torches, one in each corner of the dungeon, and open the chest in the centre to get the key before any of the torches burns out.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use the warm key to open the gate to the east.</str>
done	
done	<str>Kill Fareed to get the Smoke diamond. Protect from Melee is strongly advised and attacking with water spell or any range arrow.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Rasolo outside the house south of Baxtorian Falls.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go to the most southern tent in the Bandit camp. Bring antipoison, food, and 20+ lockpicks (you can bring noted ones and coins to exchange with Tiles in Bandit camp's general store, 5 coins for each lockpick) (For ironmen, note that both lockpicks and antipoisons may be pickpocketed from the Bandits in the vicinity).</str>
done	
done	<str>Unlock the secure chest (the 3 locks must be picked consecutively, it can take upwards of 100 tries to open the chest and is dependent upon Thieving level).</str>
done	
done	<str>Give the gilded cross to Rasolo. Even if your inventory is full, the cross will instantly be swapped for the ring.</str>
done	
done	<str>Equip the visibility ring and climb down the ladder east of Rasolo in the fenced area.</str>
done	
done	<str>Run through the dungeon, kill Damis in his 2 forms and pick up the shadow diamond (his second form drains player's prayer rapidly, it is advised to safespot Damis, this can be done by hitting a bat or rat and stacking npcs behind). Kill a Shadow Hound to complete a task in the Hard Kandarin Diary.</str>
done	
done	<str>Give your sweet food to the Troll child north-west of Trollheim by right-clicking and using the cake on the troll child.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to the Troll child.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the ice gate and kill 5 ice trolls.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the cave.</str>
done	
done	<str>Follow the path then kill Kamil (it is advised to approach with protect from magic to force him to teleport into range, then protect from melee, and manually cast your spells).</str>
done	
done	<str>Continue west and follow the long icy path.</str>
done	
done	<str>Wear spiked boots and climb the ice ledge, follow the new path.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go through the gate and smash the trolls frozen in ice by using your fire spell on each of them. Talk to them for the ice diamond.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Malak in the Canifis pub.</str>
done	
done	<str>Travel to the Draynor Sewer and give Ruantun a silver bar for a silver pot.</str>
done	
done	<str>Take the silver pot to the High Priest in the Entrana church and he will enchant it.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Malak (He will damage you for five hitpoints here, but he cannot kill you).</str>
done	
done	<str>Add spices and garlic powder to the pot of blood.</str>
done	
done	<str>Prepare for a tough boss fight (combat gear, high healing food).</str>
done	
done	<str>Go to the Morytania Graveyard north of Castle Drakan (see map).</str>
done	
done	<str>Pour your pot of blood on the tomb and defeat Dessous</str>
done	
done	<str>Return to Malak and claim the blood diamond.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go south-east of Eblis and place a diamond in each of the pyramid's obelisks.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the pyramid from the top.</str>
done	
done	<str>Run through each floor and don't stop or a trap may send you back to the start. Traps may still trigger regardless. Beware Mummies and Scarabs as they can hit over 20.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Azzanadra at the end.</str>
done	
done	<col=ff0000>QUEST COMPLETE!</col>
